# Only track what's actually needed at repo root: src/ and a handful of
# root files. Everything else at root (stray images, "Claude outputs"
# chat-delivery folder, etc.) is intentionally excluded.
#
# publish/ is deliberately NOT whitelisted below: it holds the built exe,
# pdb and distribution zips (self-contained single-file publish, so the
# exe alone is ~150 MB) - GitHub's hard per-file limit is 100 MB, and it
# doesn't belong in source-of-truth git history anyway (every build round
# would add another full-size binary blob). Ship built releases via
# GitHub Releases or Nexus instead - never commit publish/ again.
/*
!/src
!/README.md
!/liesmich.md
!/Cp77SaveManager.sln
!/build.bat
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes

# Build artifacts inside src/ - always regenerable, never worth tracking.
src/**/bin/
src/**/obj/

# Local NuGet override some dotnet commands drop when there's no network
# access to nuget.org (see README) - machine-specific, not meant to be shared.
nuget.config

# Common IDE/editor cruft, in case they ever show up under src/.
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
